skill: "crossborder-tia"
sections[3]:
  - "# crossborder-tia\n\nRun the transfer impact assessment for personal data leaving a jurisdiction: flow map, transfer mechanism, destination access risk and supplemental measures, ending in a go/no-go recommendation. Use before a new region is added to any data flow, before a vendor in another region processes personal data, and when transfer law changes.\n\nOwner: role-privacy-engineer (pod-gna, data_ai). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[5]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - search_web\n  - web_fetch\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"data flow inventory flows.toon (origin, destination, data classes); vendor list with processing locations; current transfer mechanism documents; destination country risk notes from counsel\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/privacy/tia-report.toon with flow_map[], mechanism per flow, risk_assessment[], supplemental_measures[], recommendation; approval block\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Map the flows: origin jurisdiction, destination, data classes and volume; a flow without a named legal entity on both ends is incomplete and blocks the assessment.\n2. Identify the transfer mechanism per flow (adequacy decision, standard contractual clauses, derogation); mechanism selection cites the current legal basis and its date.\n3. Assess destination access risk: government access regimes and practical precedent, using counsel's risk notes and current public sources; the assessment date is recorded because this risk moves.\n4. Inventory existing protections per flow: encryption at rest and in transit, key custody location, pseudonymization before transfer, access logging.\n5. Determine the gap between protections and the assessed risk; define supplemental measures (key custody in-origin, split processing, field-level pseudonymization) with owners and effort.\n6. Classify each flow go, go-with-measures or no-go; a no-go states what change would flip it, so the decision is reversible by evidence.\n7. Emit ask_question to role-general-counsel for mechanism validity and to role-security-auditor for the technical measure feasibility.\n8. Write tia-report.toon with the recommendation and approval block; register approved flows back into flows.toon so the next assessment starts from the register, not from memory.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\ncounsel review via role-general-counsel; technical measures to role-security-auditor.\n"
